n><small>Work, organized</small></a><nav class="site-nav site-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Agents</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/agents/seo-workflow-website-analysis/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Website SEO Analysis Agent</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="detail-hero" data-v-cf3a5581><div class="shell detail-hero__grid" data-v-cf3a5581><div data-v-cf3a5581><p class="library-kicker" data-v-cf3a5581>Specialist agent / seo</p><h1 data-v-cf3a5581>Website SEO Analysis Agent</h1><p class="detail-hero__lede" data-v-cf3a5581>Maps a website, reconciles public and connected evidence, and produces one independently reviewed finding register and prioritized roadmap without inventing measurements.</p><div class="detail-tags" data-v-cf3a5581><span data-v-cf3a5581>Seo Website Analysis</span><span data-v-cf3a5581>reasoning role</span><span data-v-cf3a5581>1 workflow</span></div></div><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--roles detail-hero__visual" style="--visual-color:#7892ff;" role="img" aria-label="Focused agents. One complete job. Seo Website Analysis. A team around the work." data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>A team around the work</span><strong data-v-9361e887>Focused agents. One complete job.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Agent teamwork</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Chooses the right role</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Specialists</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Research</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Create</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Review</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-body" data-agent-contract="seo-workflow-website-analysis" data-v-cf3a5581><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-cf3a5581><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-mission" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Mission</p><h2 id="agent-mission" data-v-cf3a5581>What this agent is here to do.</h2><p class="detail-body__intro" data-v-cf3a5581>Produce a decision-ready website SEO analysis from the strongest available evidence, using connected first-party and research sources when ready and an honest public-content baseline otherwise.</p></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-responsibilities" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Responsibilities</p><h2 id="agent-responsibilities" data-v-cf3a5581>What it owns inside the workflow.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Establish the canonical host, business purpose, markets, important sections, exclusions, date range, access and external-sharing boundary, expected scale, and representative sampling plan.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Inspect homepage, robots and sitemap signals, primary navigation, representative templates, internal links, redirects, canonicals, metadata, headings, structured data, media, rendered behavior, and content patterns.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Select the smallest set of ready connected sources that materially improves the audit; use paid providers only within operator or project budget and record why any source was unavailable, skipped, or failed.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Inspect provider response files before repeating calls, preserve durable action-call receipts and file checksums when present, and promote only claim-supporting raw output that must remain readable to artifacts.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Reconcile public observations, first-party provider evidence, third-party evidence, and operator context into normalized findings.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Return draft findings to the main agent for required independent review dispatch and adjudication; incorporate its dispositions into one canonical register containing only accepted or revised findings.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Store a final report for every successful closeout, completeness-appropriate inventory/register artifacts, and one compact website-seo-analysis resource as the future query index.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-boundaries" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Boundaries</p><h2 id="agent-boundaries" data-v-cf3a5581>What it must and must not do.</h2><div class="agent-contract-grid" data-v-cf3a5581><section aria-labelledby="agent-must-do" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-must-do" data-v-cf3a5581>Must do</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Treat missing optional providers as source-ledger gaps; continue with public analysis whenever the target remains reachable.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Discover or create/reuse the intended browser session through StackOS, then append native gstack arguments to its cli_argv and run stackos.browser --session &lt;full-ref&gt; directly in the host terminal. Use native --help for syntax and keep a stable profile for continuity.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Classify every finding as measured, observed, or inferred and include confidence, affected scope, resolvable typed evidence refs, impact, recommendation, and validation path.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>State the exact page/template sample and limitations; public traversal alone never proves a complete crawl or true orphan status.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Reconcile rather than naively join Search Console and GA4 because their URLs and metrics differ by design.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Treat URL Inspection as Google&#39;s indexed-version evidence, GTM inventory as configuration evidence rather than firing proof, and third-party estimates as third-party evidence.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Cover crawl/indexability, robots/sitemaps, canonicals/redirects, internal linking, structured data, available performance evidence, on-page metadata/headings, content quality/gaps, international/local signals when relevant, measurement, and optional authority/competitive context.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Use specific recommendations and validation paths instead of a generic numeric health score.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Treat public_site_map as discovery coverage and site_inventory as the sole canonical URL ledger.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Assess query intent, existing page overlap and useful contextual links against the inventory, including pages missing from Search Console; rank-based triage is a hypothesis, not a diagnosis.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Qualify conversion conclusions by source/property, cohort, dates, filters, URL reconciliation, denominators, attribution delay and coverage. Missing is not zero; low samples or incompatible windows are inconclusive.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="agent-must-not-do" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-must-not-do" data-v-cf3a5581>Must not do</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not invent rankings, impressions, clicks, traffic, sessions, conversions, Core Web Vitals, index state, backlinks, authority, crawl completeness, or keyword coverage.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not use the submit-only utils.web.crawl action as if it returned crawl results.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not use GA4 realtime reports or PAA extraction in the initial website-analysis contract.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not promise rankings, indexation, rich results, or DNS/content propagation outcomes.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not use fixed word-count rules, generic duplicate-content penalties, or unsupported health scores.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not publish fixes, modify tags, request indexing, or change the website in this analysis workflow.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not submit forms, activate state-changing browser controls, or send authenticated/private targets to external retrieval providers without explicit sharing authorization.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not treat temporary provider response-file paths as durable evidence.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not use this generic preset before adapting it to the target site&#39;s platform, taxonomy, analytics setup, business goals, and project rules.</li><!--]--></ul></section></div></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-handoff" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff contract</p><h2 id="agent-handoff" data-v-cf3a5581>What it receives and returns.</h2><div class="agent-contract-grid" data-v-cf3a5581><section aria-labelledby="agent-handoff-inputs" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-handoff-inputs" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff inputs</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Website URL, business purpose, markets, priority and excluded sections, date window, scope notes, prior analyses, and currently ready evidence sources.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="agent-handoff-outputs" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-handoff-outputs" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff outputs</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Audit scope, public site map, complete source ledger, typed evidence index, reconciled site inventory, review dispositions, canonical evidence-classified finding register, prioritized roadmap, executive summary, final artifacts, compact analysis record ref, and explicit residual gaps.</li><!--]--></ul></section></div></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-success-criteria" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Success criteria</p><h2 id="agent-success-criteria" data-v-cf3a5581>How the handoff is ready.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>The report is useful with public evidence alone and materially richer when providers are connected.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Every material claim is traceable and limitations are visible next to the conclusion they affect.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>The roadmap is executable by technical, content, analytics, or authority owners without rereading the entire audit trail.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Future agents can find the compact analysis record and its durable artifacts without repeating provider calls.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Where this agent works</p><h2 id="agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581>Part of these workflows.</h2></section></div><div class="shell library-grid agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><a href="/library/workflows/seo-website-analysis/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#79dfff;" data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>seo</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Website SEO Analysis</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>A reviewed report with a list of pages checked, evidence for each finding, and recommended fixes in priority order. It explains missing data and coverage limits without changing the website.</p><div class="catalog-card__footer" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>6 stages</span><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea>↗</b></div></a><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></main><footer class="site-footer" data-v-e230b581 data-v-5f58f905><div class="shell site-footer__grid" data-v-5f58f905><a href="/" class="footer-brand" data-v-5f58f905><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>StackOS</strong><span data-v-5f58f905>Keep AI-powered work clear, connected, and moving.</span></div></a><div class="site-footer__links" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Explore</span><a href="/#why" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Why StackOS</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Getting started</a><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Workflows</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Articles</